A||N||9||DaveL||Bones and Mounts||||10||
Z||000000||DaveL||02-02-2000||09:47 AM||||I started hearing a loud clunk when putting the auto trans of my 87 SE 2.5 in gear, so I had my son put it in gear while I watched, and the dogbone was in sad shape allowing the engine to shift so far the air cleaner almost hit the frame. I replaced the dogbone which solved that problem, but while I had it off, I pulled on the engine and found I could move it what seemed an axcessive amount to me. How much should one be able to move a 2.5 with the dogbone off? This motor has about 100,000 on it. Also, in 87 there appears to be only one engine mount and only one trans mount. True?||||reg||10
Z||000001||batboy||02-02-2000||10:57 AM||||My 87 SE 2.5 engine flopped around like a boneless chicken when I was replacing the dogbone on it.||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||02-02-2000||07:30 PM||||2.5's from 86.5 on with automatic transmission use only one tranny mount located to the left of the tranny below a large mettal braket.<P>These motors will move Very far without the strut in place.<P>I wish you would have read back thru other threads...... If you put in a new OEM style strut you didn't solve your problem as well as you think. The OEM mount is to weak for this tranny setup. You need Pollyurethane in at least one end or the air cleanner can still move far enough to contact the trunk wall. New OEM struts only last about 15-20k miles in these setups.||||reg||1
Z||000003||DaveL||02-03-2000||08:45 AM||||You know, I was thinking the factory OEM stuff wouldn't hold up long, especially if the rest of the mounts are played to boot. I think I'll end up getting one of those super dogbones from the Fiero Store when this one wears out. Dang  Should've done that instead. They have the other mounts, but it looks like it would cost $150 without labor. Don't have extra cash laying around. Maybe the Ex will give me some    HA||||reg||1
Z||000004||batboy||02-03-2000||10:45 AM||||Ogre must be harder on his dogbones, maybe because of more stop and go traffic. I got 30,000 miles out of my last factory style 1987 2.5 dogbone. The point is that they wear fast. Those poly ultimate dogbones are well worth the extra cash in the long run.||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||02-03-2000||08:12 PM||||Bat's isn't yours a stick? This particular problem is with automatics. The stick cars all have 2 tranny mounts. the auto's after 86.5 have only one. that leaves the motor and tranny a total, including the strut, of 3 mounting points as oposed to 4 for the stick or the older auto's. The 2 mounts on the tranny did allot of torque damping even before the strut is added. with the sinlge mount the entire load goes thru the strut.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||02-03-2000||11:54 PM||||Ogre, I know it's hard to keep track of all three of my Fieros. My 85 GT is a 4 speed, but my V8 Batmobile (85 SE) and my 87 SE are both automatics. The 87 SE presently has a dead 2.5 engine, but before it died last summer, I had put over 60,000 miles on it in a little over 3 years. It's was my 1987 four banger that I was referring to in this post.||||reg||1
Z||000007||DaveL||02-04-2000||10:38 AM||||After all is said and done, I'll check to see if either of the other mounts is broken. I'm not going through the expense and hassle of replacement unless one is. Dogbones are cheap and really easy to replace. Thanks for the input from all of you. Some folks I know bought this 87 SE 2.5 DIS with auto and gave it to their 18 year old. He racked up $600 worth of speeding tickets and violations in three months. They took it back and sold it to me for the price of the tickets. Not a bad deal. Little did I know how much I would enjoy this "poor mans' Porsche". Now I'm in the middle of trying to tackle the electrical problems with this particular car. You'll be hearing more from me.||||reg||1
Z||000008||theogre||02-04-2000||11:07 AM||||It's not hard to change either mount. especially the tranny if you have a long extension. I don't know what they cost. They are pretty floppy. They are only there to hold up the motor. the don't do much else.||||reg||1
Z||000009||mshill||02-04-2000||03:07 PM||||Since I have my engine out for the rebuild, I an replacing all mounts and already have poly in the bone.<BR>||||reg||1
